 "lines": [],
 "notes": "Vulcan Rock is the exposed top of a granite tor in a cluster of pinnacles trending north-west to south-east, off the Karbonkelberg coast beyond the mouth of Hout Bay; there is no shore within the drawing. The rock position is the OpenStreetMap seamark (node 3662683982); the North Ridge, West Ridge and Rocksucker Ridge positions, the cavern at 15-20 m under the rock, the balloon-cave overhang, the 28-30 m sand patch to the south-west, the low reef at 24 m to the west, the kelp line and the advice not to anchor come from the Wikivoyage 'Diving the Cape Peninsula and False Bay/Vulcan Rock' guide. The outlines of the ridges, the kelp and the sand patch and the boat drop are drawn around those points and are approximate.",
